        "id": 5434209468,
        "body": "> [!WARNING]\n> Copilot couldn't run its full agentic review because it didn't start before the timeout. Make sure your repository has a runner available, or add a `copilot-code-review.yml` file specifying one with the `runs-on` attribute. See the [docs](https://gh.io/AA11tgch) for more details.\n\n<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n## Copilot review overview\n\n**Review effort:** Lite  \n**Findings:** 1 <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.png\" alt=\"High severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture>\n\n<details open>\n<summary><strong>Open (1)</strong></summary>\n\n- <picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.svg\"><img src=\"https://github.githubassets.com/static/images/icons/copilot-code-review/high-v2-light.png\" alt=\"High severity\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" align=\"texttop\"></picture> [This immutable-input guard hard-codes files that the workflow itself classifies as absent for\u2026](#discussion_r4200122706) \u00b7 New\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n\nCarries shared validation / review setup fixes back into the PowerShell repo, including a dedicated Copilot review-prep workflow, improved metadata/finalization self-tests, and Markdown parser structural reuse/strict conversion safeguards.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Adds a dedicated `copilot-code-review.yml` workflow (review-only setup) plus related validator updates to treat it as an optional governed input.\n- Introduces bounded Markdown parse structural snapshot reuse and a native JSON structural converter path with comprehensive self-tests.\n- Updates CI helper tests/fixtures, timeouts, KaTeX override documentation, and a few metadata/version annotations.\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| docs/\u200bdependency-maintenance.md | Documents KaTeX override rationale/constraints and updates metadata date. |\r\n| .github/\u200bworkflows/\u200bscripts-README.md | Updates metadata date. |\r\n| .github/\u200bworkflows/\u200bpackage.json | Adds an npm `overrides` entry to pin KaTeX under a specific parent. |\r\n| .github/\u200bworkflows/\u200bcopilot-code-review.yml | Adds dedicated Copilot review preparation workflow (locked tool setup / guards, no aggregate validation). |\r\n| .github/\u200bworkflows/\u200bagent-instructions.yml | Extends job/step timeouts for instruction/workflow behavior testing. |\r\n| .github/\u200bworkflows/\u200bTest-StyleGuideArtifacts.ps1 | Updates versions and corrects output type annotation for artifact parsing. |\r\n| .github/\u200bworkflows/\u200bTest-CiHelpers.test.mjs | Updates fixtures/tests for Git discovery via required PowerShell 7 and validates new review workflow behavior parity. |\r\n| .github/\u200bworkflows/\u200bTest-AgentInstructions.ps1 | Adds optional review workflow input handling, structural reuse plumbing, and native JSON structural conversion option. |\r\n| .github/\u200bworkflows/\u200bTest-AgentInstructions.SelfTest.ps1 | Adds/extends self-tests for native conversion parity, reuse behavior, and finalization/clock handling. |\n</details>\n\n<details>\n<summary>Files not reviewed (1)</summary>\n\n* **.github/workflows/package-lock.json**: Generated file\n</details>\n\n---\n\n\ud83d\udca1 <a href=\"/franklesniak/PSStyleGuide/new/main?filename=.github/skills/code-review/SKILL.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a `code-review` agent skill</a> or configure MCP servers for context-aware, tailored reviews. <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/use-copilot-agents/request-a-code-review/use-code-review?tool=webui#mcp-servers-and-agent-skills\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Learn more in the docs.</a>",
        "state": "COMMENTED",
