      {
        "pull_request_review_id": 5434209468,
        "id": 4200122706,
        "path": ".github/workflows/copilot-code-review.yml",
        "body": "This immutable-input guard hard-codes files that the workflow itself classifies as absent for legacy/node-only layouts (e.g., `package.json`, `requirements-dev.txt`, `ci-toolchain.json`). In those layouts, `git diff ... -- <missing path>` will fail with a pathspec error, causing the workflow to fail even though the earlier `Detect locked validation-tool layout` step explicitly allows those inputs to be absent. Make `setup_inputs` conditional on `steps.toolchain.outputs.layout` / `steps.toolchain.outputs.validation` (mirroring the later immutable list logic), so legacy runs only check `.github/workflows/package*.json` (and any other guaranteed-present files), while modern/full runs check the expanded set.",
